.TH photocraft-cli-mcp 1  "mcp " 
.SH NAME
photocraft\-cli\-mcp \- Run the MCP server on stdio (headless engine, or bridge to a running `photocraft \-\-control <port>`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBphotocraft\-cli mcp\fR [\fB\-\-bridge\fR] [\fB\-\-gpu\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-gpu\fR] [\fB\-\-control\-token\fR] [\fB\-\-control\-token\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-automation\-read\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-automation\-write\-root\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the MCP server on stdio (headless engine, or bridge to a running `photocraft \-\-control <port>`)
.PP
Headless: each automation root grants that direction of file access; an omitted root denies it. Prefer absolute root paths in MCP client configurations. Bridge: set the roots on the desktop app; root flags are refused. The token flags require \-\-bridge (or PHOTOCRAFT_CONTROL_PORT).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-bridge\fR \fI<127.0.0.1:PORT>\fR
Bridge to the PhotoCraft app listening here instead of a headless engine; a bare port means 127.0.0.1:<PORT>
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPHOTOCRAFT_CONTROL_PORT\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-gpu\fR
Prefer GPU rendering, falling back to CPU when unavailable or unsupported
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-gpu\fR
Use CPU rendering, overriding PHOTOCRAFT_GPU
.TP
\fB\-\-control\-token\fR \fI<64\-HEX>\fR
The control token (64 hex digits)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPHOTOCRAFT_CONTROL_TOKEN\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-control\-token\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
A file holding the control token, used instead of \-\-control\-token (a server creates it when missing)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPHOTOCRAFT_CONTROL_TOKEN_FILE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-automation\-read\-root\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
The folder automation may read from (none without it)
.TP
\fB\-\-automation\-write\-root\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
The folder automation may write to (none without it)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
